> Conclusion

Factorisation can reduce work under explicit structural assumptions; BN adds moving state;
label smoothing changes the fitted target distribution. The separate arithmetic, gradient,
state and shape checks establish those mechanisms. The two compact CIFAR-10 fits
report held-out predictions from their validation-selected checkpoints.

> References

- [Ioffe and Szegedy (2015), Batch Normalization](https://arxiv.org/abs/1502.03167).
- [Szegedy et al. (2016), Rethinking the Inception Architecture for Computer Vision](https://arxiv.org/abs/1512.00567).
- [TF-Slim Inception v2](https://github.com/tensorflow/models/blob/master/research/slim/nets/inception_v2.py).
- [TF-Slim Inception v3](https://github.com/tensorflow/models/blob/master/research/slim/nets/inception_v3.py).
- [CIFAR-10 dataset and binary-file layout](https://www.cs.toronto.edu/~kriz/cifar.html).
